"""Layer-0 MLP down-projection component 5334 (partial explanation).

It fires on the head word right after a possessive determiner (his, her, my, your, our,
their) or after the genitive 's: "his [wife]", "your [answer]", "Dyer's [daughter]".
Its sign depends on the word:
- people and family nouns (wife, husband, son, daughter, students, customers): strongly negative;
- nouns for one's own output (work, answer, analysis, reasoning, results): strongly negative;
- nouns for roles, duties and status (name, task, job, position, right, responsibility,
  part, problem, case): positive;
- any other word after a possessive: slightly negative.
Everywhere else it is ~0. Word lists are conceptual groups; the program does not model the
diffuse background (about two thirds of the variance) or the rest of the context.
"""
